{"name":"Knapsack","hex":"#95896c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"knapsack","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A case of canvas or leather, for carrying items on the back.","A set of values from which a subset is chosen."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To go hiking while burdened with a knapsack, usually overnight or for longer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knapsack"}],"entries":[{"title":"Knapsack (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Knapsack is an American rock band formed in 1993 by Blair Shehan (vocals/guitar) and Colby Mancasola (drums). Shehan and Mancasola were two high school friends studying at the University of California, Davis. Guitarist Jason Bokros and bass guitarist Rod Meyer completed the line-up."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/15-05-01_Groezrock_Knapsack_02.jpg/330px-15-05-01_Groezrock_Knapsack_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knapsack_(band)","wikidata":"Q3815907"},{"title":"Backpack","blocks":[{"text":"A backpack, also called knapsack, schoolbag, rucksack, pack, booksack, bookbag, haversack, packsack, or backsack, is in its simplest frameless form, a fabric sack carried on one’s back and secured with two straps that go over the shoulders, and is used to carry goods from one place to another. It can feature an external or internal frame to transfer heavy loads off the user’s shoulders and onto their hips, reducing strain and increasing comfort on long hikes with heavy gear."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Rucksack1.jpg/330px-Rucksack1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backpack","wikidata":"Q5843"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Canon-Deluxe_Backpack-200-EG.jpg/500px-Canon-Deluxe_Backpack-200-EG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org